  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Widespread soaking rain expected Thursday. Some\ndrought relief is possible, though flooding is not expected.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure exits across the Maritimes tonight while an \noccluded front approaches from the west. An area of rain will \nbegin to expand eastward across the forecast area tonight in \nadvance of the front. A disturbance moving around an upper low \nacross Quebec province will help support a developing low along \nthe front Thursday. Rain will occur regionwide Thursday. The \ndeveloping low will cross the Gulf of Maine Thursday night. \nRain chances will begin to diminish later Thursday night. The \nsurface low exits across the Maritimes Friday, with a trof\nextending back across the forecast area, while the upper low \nbegins to move south across the region. Showers will persist \nacross the region Friday, with the better chances across \nnorthern areas. Could also have the slight chance of a \nthunderstorm Friday afternoon. The surface/upper lows vertically\nstack across the Maritimes Friday night into Saturday, slowing \nthe movement of the system. A disturbance moving around the \nMaritimes system will rotate across the region Saturday. Shower \nchances will persist Friday night into Saturday. The system then\nexits Saturday night into Sunday. The entire forecast area \nshould receive a soaking rain later Wednesday night into \nThursday night. Generally expect rainfall totals of a half to \nthree quarters of an inch across much of the forecast area \nWednesday night into Saturday, with areas of up to around an \ninch.",
